<Article
  locale="en"
  page="about"
  title="About this converter | HEIC to JPG"
  description="A free HEIC converter that runs in your browser, made by the photo book company foto foto."
  h1="About this converter"
  updated="Last updated 29 August 2026"
>
  <p>
    We build <a href="https://fotofoto.app" rel="noopener">foto foto</a>, which turns
    a folder of photos into a printed photo book without asking anyone to lay out a
    page. Almost every folder we are handed starts as HEIC, because almost every
    photo starts on an iPhone.
  </p>
  <p>
    So we already had a HEIC decoder that runs in the browser, and we already
    believed that a stranger's photographs should not have to travel to a server to
    change file format. This page is that decoder, given its own address and made
    free for anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>What it does differently</h2>
  <p>
    Two things, both small and both the reason it exists.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      It converts on your own machine. Every other converter near the top of this
      search sends your photos away and sends different files back.
    </li>
    <li>
      It keeps the date the photo was taken. Most converters stamp the JPG with the
      moment you converted it, which quietly flattens a holiday into an afternoon.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What it costs</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing, and there is no tier that costs something. It is free because it is
    cheap for us to run, since there is no server doing the work, and because
    people who have just untangled a folder of photos are occasionally people who
    would like a book made out of them.
  </p>

  <h2>Who made it</h2>
  <p>
    foto foto, based in the Netherlands. You can reach us at
    <a href="mailto:hello@fotofoto.app">hello@fotofoto.app</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Open source</h2>
  <p>
    The whole converter is on
    <a href="https://github.com/kayamy/heictojpg" rel="noopener">GitHub</a> under
    the MIT licence. Read it, run it yourself, or check that the no-upload claim
    holds by watching the network tab.
  </p>

  <p>
